    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nTwo files, following the existing endpoint pattern:\n\n1. **New step class** `CheckEmailDomain.java` \u2014 a single-method function that reads the built `Owner`, extracts the email domain, and throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"email\"))` when it's in the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). An absent email is left untouched.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkEmailDomain` step right after `build` in the pipeline.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- The reject-with-400 behavior reuses the **existing** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsHandler` 400 path \u2014 the exact path `BuildOwner` already uses for a malformed email. So no new exception, handler, or escalation YAML was needed.\n- The new logic lives in a brand-new single-method class, so its `WMC_other` is zero (no surrounding class complexity to carry), and no existing Java method was edited \u2014 I didn't grow `BuildOwner` (whose `toE164` helper would have inflated `WMC_other`).\n- Total footprint: one new small class plus one YAML wiring edit.",
